;;; M1a S1a.6.6 — a `(query :goal …)` whose relation head is a variable.
;;;
;;; Two lines, and the shortest find the fuzzer has produced. `(?R Rex
;;; Animal)` is the same shape the compiler rejects inside a rule — M1 matches
;;; relations per activator (Q29), so a head variable must be bound by one —
;;; but a *query* goal has no activator at all, so it can never be bound and
;;; the pattern is uncompilable by construction.
;;;
;;; The goal is compiled only where a model is rendered: after the solve and
;;; before the table, the CLI asks `verdict::goal_plan_error` whether the goal
;;; compiles. It does not, so the run prints no table and exits 1 with one
;;; stderr line:
;;;
;;;     ein.inference.compile.CompileError: unbound relation head ?R …
;;;
;;; Fixed 2026-08-20 in ein.rs, which until then returned no bindings and
;;; printed "(no query goal to project)" — running a program it should have
;;; refused. `saturate` answers, because it ignores the query, and `render
;;; rules` rejects the file for its own reason (it has no rule forms).
;;;
;;; `query-goal-free-head-unsat.ein` is the sibling that renders no model,
;;; and so never compiles the goal.

(is-a Rex Animal)

(query
  :goal (?R Rex Animal))
